    "title": "Kansas basketball vs California Baptist start time, TV channel, info",
    "text": "March 20, 2026, 4:04 a.m. CTSAN DIEGO, California — Kansas basketball’s stay in the men’s NCAA tournament begins Friday with a game in the round of 64 against California Baptist.The Jayhawks (23-10) are the No. 4 seed in the East Region, while the Lancers (25-8) are the No. 13 seed. KU is coming off of a trip to the semifinals of the Big 12 Conference tournament. California Baptist is coming off of a Western Athletic Conference tournament championship.Here’s how fans can follow along with this game, with tipoff set for 8:45 p.m. (CT) at the Viejas Arena:What channel is Kansas basketball vs California Baptist game on today?TV channel: CBSLivestream: FuboKansas basketball’s game against California Baptist will be broadcast on CBS during the 2025-26 season. Streaming options include Fubo. The winner will advance to face either No. 5 seed St. John’s or No. 12 seed Northern Iowa.Kansas basketball vs California BaptistDate: Friday, March 20Start time: 8:45 p.m. (CT)Kansas basketball will play California Baptist at 8:45 p.m. (CT) in San Diego, California.Watch Kansas basketball vs California BaptistKansas basketball vs California Baptist score predictionKansas has been up and down of late, especially during the Big 12 tournament. However, the Jayhawks are going to be the favorite heading into this NCAA tournament matchup. Look for Kansas to coast to a 78-61 win.Kansas basketball 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at Kansas’ last three games:March 7 (home): Kansas State — Kansas won 104-85March 12 (neutral): TCU — Kansas won 78-73March 13 (neutral): Houston — Kansas lost 69-47California Baptist 2025-26 scheduleHere’s a look at California Baptist’s last three games:March 7 (away): Southern Utah University — California Baptist won 82-75March 13 (neutral): Utah Tech — California Baptist won 86-72March 14 (neutral): Utah Valley University — California Baptist won 63-61Jordan Guskey covers University of Kansas Athletics at The Topeka Capital-Journal. He was the 2022 National Sports Media Association’s sportswriter of the year for the state of Kansas. Contact him at jmguskey@gannett.com or on Twitter at @JordanGuskey.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
